What is the output of the following Java program demonstrating stack unwinding across method boundaries?
```java
public class UnwindDemo {
    static void stepA() {
        System.out.print("A1 ");
        stepB();
        System.out.print("A2 ");
    }
    static void stepB() {
        System.out.print("B1 ");
        throw new IllegalStateException("Stop");
    }
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        try {
            stepA();
        } catch (IllegalStateException e) {
            System.out.print("Caught");
        }
    }
}
```

